# =========================================================================
# Debian package control file
# =========================================================================
# TEACHING NOTE: The control file is the metadata header of a .deb package.
# When you run "dpkg -I package.deb", this is what gets displayed. It tells
# the dpkg/apt system:
#   - What the package is called (Package)
#   - What it depends on (Depends)
#   - Who maintains it (Maintainer)
#   - What architecture it runs on (Architecture)
#   - A short and long description
#
# This file is used by dpkg-deb when building the package. The fields here
# map directly to CPACK_DEBIAN_* variables in packaging.cmake, but having
# a standalone control file lets us build .deb packages manually with
# dpkg-deb if needed (without CMake/CPack).
#
# Field reference:
#   Source       - The source package name (for building from source)
#   Section      - Category in the Debian archive (web, net, utils, etc.)
#   Priority     - optional is standard for user-facing apps
#   Maintainer   - Who is responsible for this package
#   Build-Depends - Packages needed to compile (not needed in CPack output)
#   Package      - The binary package name (what users install)
#   Architecture - any = arch-independent (scripts, docs); or specific arch
#   Depends      - Runtime dependencies (installed automatically by apt)
#   Description  - First line: short summary. Following lines: long description
#                 (indented with a space, blank lines use " .")
# =========================================================================

Source: chinstrap
Section: web
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Chinstrap Project <chinstrap@example.com>
Build-Depends: cmake, g++, make, libx11-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.0
Homepage: https://github.com/chinstrap/chinstrap

Package: chinstrap
Architecture: any
Depends: libx11-6, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: A from-scratch web browser with zero third-party libraries
 Chinstrap is a web browser written entirely in C++17 with no external
 dependencies. It implements its own HTML parser, CSS engine, JavaScript
 interpreter, TLS stack, HTTP client, and rendering pipeline from scratch.
 .
 Features:
  * HTML5 parsing
  * CSS3 parsing and layout
  * JavaScript ES6 interpreter
  * TLS 1.2/1.3 encryption
  * HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 support
  * DNS resolution
  * Cookie management
  * Disk cache
  * X11 display backend